cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Affine-Bundle Solvers for General Linear Equality Systems:
  Independently Verifiable Nearby-Status Certificates and
  Information-Adaptive Routing
message: >-
  If you use this software or refer to its results, please cite
  this archived software release.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Viktor
    family-names: Mikhalkin
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0000-4954-2300'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/metronforge/affine-bundle-solver'
abstract: >-
  A dense solver architecture for real linear equality systems Ax=b that
  assumes neither consistency, full rank, nor uniqueness. The state is an
  affine bundle whose canonical coordinates support an exact insertion
  calculus separating redundancy from contradiction. In finite precision the
  router reports a status, an epistemic strength, a supported numerical-rank
  interval, and a fixed-solution quality quantity, leaving rows near a rank
  transition unresolved rather than forcing a binary decision. A separate
  strict checker derives outward perturbation bounds from the source data and
  independently verifies three typed proof objects for exact uniqueness,
  exact consistency with nonuniqueness, and exact inconsistency.
keywords:
  - linear systems
  - certified computation
  - numerical rank
  - consistency classification
  - affine bundle
  - certifying algorithms
  - verified numerical linear algebra
license: Apache-2.0
